Your security team creates a custom Azure Policy definition to deny the creation of storage accounts that allow public blob access. During testing, storage accounts with `allowBlobPublicAccess` set to `true` are still being created successfully. You review the policy definition JSON:

```json
{
  "mode": "All",
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {
          "field": "type",
          "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"
        },
        {
          "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/allowBlobPublicAccess",
          "equals": "true"
        }
      ]
    },
    "then": {
      "effect": "audit"
    }
  }
}
```

What change must you make to the policy definition so that non-compliant storage accounts are blocked at creation time?

Your team uses Defender for Cloud with DevOps security enabled. A pull request to your infrastructure repository triggers an automated annotation flagging a Key Vault resource definition for a missing security configuration. You review the Bicep file:

```bicep
resource keyVault 'Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults@2023-02-01' = {
  name: 'kv-prod-001'
  location: resourceGroup().location
  properties: {
    sku: {
      family: 'A'
      name: 'standard'
    }
    tenantId: subscription().tenantId
    accessPolicies: []
    enableRbacAuthorization: true
    softDeleteRetentionInDays: 90
  }
}
```

Defender for Cloud recommends adding a property to prevent network-level exposure of the vault. Which property should you add to the `properties` block?

Your team is configuring a Data Collection Rule (DCR) to ingest JSON logs from an in-house service into a custom table in the Sentinel workspace. A colleague has drafted the following DCR stream declaration and `transformKql` snippet.

```json
{
  "streamDeclarations": {
    "Custom-InHouseService_CL": {
      "columns": [
        { "name": "TimeGenerated", "type": "datetime" },
        { "name": "EventMessage",  "type": "string" },
        { "name": "Severity",      "type": "string" }
      ]
    }
  },
  "dataFlows": [
    {
      "streams": ["Custom-InHouseService_CL"],
      "destinations": ["myWorkspace"],
      "outputStream": "InHouseService_CL",
      "transformKql": "source | project EventMessage, Severity"
    }
  ]
}
```

What should be corrected?
